  "scope": "Explicit FullRegionV2 enlargement requests capture complete area geometry through a closed nested-attribute codec with intrinsic packed extents and signed XY origins. Borrowed admission includes complete output/record/publication bounds and the whole Python/JSON transport depth, including typed string arrays. Validation recomputes the original full equation before replay/rebind; equality includes frame origin. Captured guards, current Previous, cancellation and finish failure preserve atomic publication. Preparation freezes the admitted command before C++ callbacks can replace their source value. Empty masks, shrink-erased originals and zero-distance commands preserve exact source storage and avoid spurious selection revisions. The shared ImGui dialog now records V2; explicit action geometry selects full mode and recorded rebind controls retain it. Existing programmatic defaults and historical V1 records retain their original clipped equations. Portable authored intent, V2 capture adoption/inference, JSON programs, actual workflow controls, generic filtering and session batches retain full regions across repeated edits and V4 reopen. Downstream histogram/contrast, Boolean/rotation, saved ROI geometry, axis/planar transforms and ImageJ interchange still require migration. This is not complete editor interoperability or platform certification.",
