    "reference": "The unchanged full ImageJ 1.54r fixture supplies 144 complete stages over 72 two-step sequences. Commands validate/replay/publish/reopen each stage for pixel and calibrated units. These tests transport existing observations; they do not count new independent oracle data.",
    "actual_ui": "One actual-input Python launch case expands/shrinks an off-image corner through the shared native ImGui dialog, confirms both captured workflow steps, prepares/keeps a portable program, then runs/applies it. Final program and applied-frame reports are retained. Existing C++ dialog native tests also run the migrated V2 dialog over three centered scalar/RGB/IEEE recipes. Three installed standalone app probes are regression evidence, not new off-image standalone launch certification.",
    "failed_attempts": "Retained native preimage reproduces command reassignment during callbacks switching the prepared document. Initial new tests incorrectly expected an erased V1 shrink to become empty, expected batch staging to leave the output directory entirely empty, and confirmed only one of two workflow entries; corrected only those new assumptions, preserving all reference data and historical expectations. Additional regressions observed late rejection of nested V2 metadata after callbacks, then a freshly resolved native record failing whole-root Python re-entry. V2 now counts the complete transport and typed string arrays before callbacks. A generation005 matrix passed, but a final semantic audit reproduced empty/erased legacy masks spuriously changing storage kind; kernel identity is now preserved and four new exact-no-op cases pass in generation006."
